From b5e1195b31e565785c6951d9855446bf0e53ca78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 18:10:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 523/572] fix(st-usb): use const pointers for function
 parameters when not modified

Some functions use pointer as parameter but do not modify the object it
points to. Use const in that case.
This corrects MISRA_C_2012_Rule_8.13 warning:
A pointer should point to a const-qualified type whenever possible

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 57da49e8d4780bcbd0b1d4a0a9e72bdb6411ccc5 fix(st-usb): use const pointers for function parameters when not modified]
Change-Id: I5400c01d4ba12220d7dbd0af59afeb2934227ec7
